00:13:18.079 --> 00:13:21.769
And Brett Beyer does a decent job at fact
checking him in real time.

00:13:21.769 --> 00:13:25.870
But I thought that Bear especially did well
at the end there by emphasizing the fact that

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:31.110
his question was about how do you win over
an undecided female independent voter who

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.370
didn't vote for you in 2020?

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:37.850
And your response has been to complain about
voter fraud, even though the public is tired

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:39.830
of hearing about this issue?

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:41.389
It's not a winning issue for you.

00:13:41.389 --> 00:13:44.890
It's not a voting issue for people, independents
especially.

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:46.260
It's not policy.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.380
You're not being convincing when you talk
about this.

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:49.630
It's uninspiring.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:51.930
And then Trump tries to course correct.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:56.180
But instead of doing it in the standard way
of talking about, you know, the normal policy

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.910
issues, the economy, the border, guns, even
culture war stuff, if you want to get into

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:01.910
it.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:05.750
Instead, he diverts into talking about how
he's winning in all the polls.

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:08.360
So people should vote for him because he's
winning.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.209
Like, how does this add up?

00:14:10.209 --> 00:14:11.380
How does this follow logically?

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:15.200
So Trump's appeal to the independent voter
who didn't vote for him in 2020 is number

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:16.200
one.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.040
The election was rigged in 2020 and it was
unfairly stolen for me.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.810
Therefore, I deserve another term.

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:27.490
And number two, I'm winning in the polls already,
so you should vote for me because I'm winning.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:32.459
So I got to say, this guy doesn't look like
his normal self.

00:14:32.459 --> 00:14:34.060
He seems a little bit rattled.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:37.920
I'm sure he's worried about the possibility
of serving time in prison.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:41.990
I'm sure he's worried about the possibility
of not winning an election again because it

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:45.279
devastated him so much the last time that
happened.

00:14:45.279 --> 00:14:47.240
Maybe I'm looking too much into the body language.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.589
Maybe I'm looking too much into the facial
expressions.

00:14:49.589 --> 00:14:53.970
But to me, this seems like a very concerned
man who doesn't have the poise and the confidence

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:55.509
that he normally does.

00:14:55.509 --> 00:14:56.620
That's Donald Trump.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.110
For you right now.

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:02.000
Not feeling his best, I got to say, and not
getting the best end end of this exchange

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.000
with Brett Baer.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.000
All right.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.000
We're going to go to a break now.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:16:13.339
We'll be back with much more of the David
Pakman show on 

00:16:13.339 --> 00:16:32.060
the 

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:41.079
other side.

